+Three integration tests budget the mock provider's credits so that the key runs out part-way. Each now allows one
+credit more, for the Dairy & Eggs category page the SYNTHETIC Food page links:
+`test_scrapedo_walmart.py::test_an_exhausted_key_stops_the_run_resumably_and_nothing_else_is_tried`,
+`test_operations.py::test_a_complete_run_is_published_and_a_partial_run_never_replaces_it` and the partial run of
+`test_publication_safety.py`. They pass on 1.6.7 and 1.6.8 alike.
+
+One integration test names the category pages a run requests:
+`test_coverage_and_assortment.py::test_the_category_page_is_read_through_the_general_api_never_the_store_plugin`
+now expects the Dairy & Eggs category page as well as the Food page, each through the general API, never the store
+plugin. It fails on 1.6.7, which never requests the Dairy & Eggs page. The first 1.6.8 commit (`745607e`) still
+expected the Food page alone and failed this test; the full Linux suite on the owner's VM found it on 2026-11-05,
+before any archive of that commit was delivered.
+
+The second 1.6.8 commit (`7a96218`) was then replayed on the stored pages of L12 (on the workstation,
+2026-11-05; no request). Beside the agreed renames ("Fabric Softener" to "Fabric Softeners", the name the
+Household Essentials page gives the listing), it renamed carried records after a second link the same page
+gives the same listing: "Subscription" for the cough and cold medicine listing, "Men's Deodorant" for
+Deodorant and "Great Value Pantry" for Pantry. The third commit (`9c14425`) read such a listing once and kept
+the first name the page gives it. No archive of `7a96218` was delivered.
+
+The third commit's rule was then checked against the full URLs of the 1,505 links the stored category pages
+record (on the workstation, 2026-11-05; no request), and it did not hold: its key took only the listing ID.
+"Subscription" and "Men's Deodorant" are not second names of a listing but filtered views of it (a facet in the
+link's query), and two different shelves share the listing ID `0`. The rows above replace it: only two links to
+one view of a listing are one read; a filtered link has the listing itself read, in full. A run can read more
+than before, since a listing linked only filtered is now read whole. Every test named in those rows fails on
+`9c14425` by the message quoted, and passes on the fourth commit. No archive of `9c14425` was delivered, and no
